# Networking configuration (copy to .env.local for local dev; set these as
# GitHub repo secrets for the Pages build). ALL are optional — with none set,
# the app uses public STUN + the PeerJS cloud broker (direct P2P).
#
# WARNING: VITE_* vars are inlined into the public client bundle and are
# readable by anyone who loads the page. Use short-lived / ephemeral TURN
# credentials (TURN REST API) rather than permanent ones where possible.

# --- TURN relay (optional; only needed for strict NATs or IP hiding) ---
# Comma-separated TURN URLs. Prefer TLS (turns:) so it survives strict networks.
VITE_TURN_URLS="turns:your.turn.host:5349?transport=tcp,turn:your.turn.host:3478?transport=udp"
VITE_TURN_USERNAME="your-turn-username"
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL="your-turn-credential"

# Relay-only (iceTransportPolicy: "relay") is DISABLED in code: forcing all peer
# traffic through TURN silently broke every connection on the deployed build when
# TURN was even slightly misconfigured (while local dev kept working). TURN above
# is used as a non-exclusive fallback instead, so connections always have a path.
# This var is currently IGNORED. To hide IPs you need a verified, always-on TURN
# server; only then re-enable the relay path in iceConfig() (see net.ts).
# VITE_ICE_RELAY_ONLY="true"  # (ignored — see net.ts)

# --- Custom PeerJS signaling server (optional) ---
# The default PeerJS cloud broker can be flaky. Point at your own PeerServer if
# needed. Leave unset to use the default cloud.
# VITE_PEER_HOST="your.peerserver.host"
# VITE_PEER_PORT="443"
# VITE_PEER_PATH="/"
# VITE_PEER_KEY="peerjs"
# VITE_PEER_SECURE="true"
